import Foundation

/// Extracts #tags from a note's body text, in the order they appear.
///
/// A tag is a `#` followed by one or more letters, digits, underscores, or
/// hyphens. Surrounding punctuation (e.g. "(#ideas)", "list,#urgent.") is
/// ignored, and tags are returned in the order they appear in the text.
public func extractTags(from text: String) -> [String] {
    let pattern = /#[A-Za-z0-9_-]+/
    return text.matches(of: pattern).map { String(text[$0.range].dropFirst()) }
}
```

Check: `text.matches(of:)` — String has `matches(of:)` via SE-0351: `func matches
<R>(of regex: R) -> [R.MatchedSubstring] where R: RegexComponent`. MatchedSubstring
 is a generic `RegexComponent` with `range: Range<Subject.Index>`. For a String subject
, Index = String.Index. So `text[$0.range]` works.

