Protocol { func matches<R>(of regex: R) ... }` — availability: iOS 16.0, macOS 13
.0, etc. We have .v13 so no problem.

Or, to be completely safe, use NSRegularExpression. But since the platform is .v1
3, the regex literal is fine. I'll try the literal first, and fall back if it fails
 to compile.

